me became cult hits like Pixies, The Replacements, and The Smiths.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Tame Impala", "streams": 3354, "best_position": 14}, {"artist": "Noize MC", "streams": 2139, "best_position": 46}, {"artist": "The Neighbourhood", "streams": 1782, "best_position": 74}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Avril Lavigne", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bad Omens", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bring Me the Horizon", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Cocteau Twins", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Coldplay", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Crystal Castles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "classic rock": {"genre": "classic rock", "country_code": "by", "country_name": "Belarus", "summary": "Classic rock was originally conceived as a radio station programming format which evolved from the album oriented rock (AOR) format in the early-1980s. In the United States, this rock music format now features a large playlist of songs ranging from the 1960s, 1970s, 1980s and early 1990s, with some stations including a limited number of current releases.\n\nThe classic rock stations recreate the sound of Album Oriented Rock (AOR) stations of the 60s-90s (although usually with a much more limited playlist) and appeal mainly to adults.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "David Bowie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Pink Floyd", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Queen", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Scorpions", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Beatles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "dance-pop": {"genre": "dance-pop", "country_code": "by", "country_name": "Belarus", "summary": "Dance-pop is a style of electronic dance music and a subgenre of pop music that evolved from Disco, circa 1981, that combines dance beats with a pop/R'n'B song structure. Because there is such an emphasis on fully-formed songs in dance-pop, it's often viewed as a separate classification unto itself apart from pure dance. Dance-pop is also closely related to the teen pop and Eurodance movements in the mid-1980s and late 1990s, the rise of boy bands and girl groups, and the reintroduction of the vocoder and similar such innovations.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Addison Rae", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Kim Petras", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Madonna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electronic": {"genre": "electronic", "country_code": "by", "country_name": "Belarus", "summary": "Electronic music refers to music that emphasizes the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic music technology as a central aspect of the sound of the music. Historically, electronic music was considered to be any music created with the use of electronic musical instruments or electronic processing, but in modern times, that distinction has been lost because almost all recorded music today, and the majority of live music performances, depend on extensive use of electronics.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artis